### 4.4 Persistence Layer

Implement a `Storage` module that wraps `localStorage`:

```javascript
const Storage = {
  save(key, value) { localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(value)); },
  load(key, defaultValue) {
    try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key)) ?? defaultValue; }
    catch { return defaultValue; }
  },
  remove(key) { localStorage.removeItem(key); }
};
```

Persist the following to `localStorage`:
- All workspace metadata and file contents (key: `workspaces`)
- User settings (key: `settings`)
- Theme preference (key: `theme`)
- Recent files per workspace (key: `recent_files`)
- Terminal command history per workspace (key: `terminal_history`)

