## 5. Initialization Sequence

The `<script type="module">` block must execute the following sequence on `DOMContentLoaded`:

1. Load settings from `localStorage` and apply them (theme, font size, etc.)
2. Initialize the `ThemeManager` and apply the saved theme
3. Initialize the `Router` and parse the current URL hash
4. Render the appropriate view into `#root`
5. If the view is the workspace view, initialize the `EditorView` (CodeMirror 6) and mount it into `.editor-pane`
6. Initialize the xterm.js `Terminal` instance, attach `FitAddon`, and mount it into `.terminal-body`
7. Call `fitAddon.fit()` and set up a `ResizeObserver` on the terminal container to call `fitAddon.fit()` on resize
8. Restore open files and active file from `localStorage`
9. Restore terminal command history from `localStorage`
10. Register all global keyboard shortcut listeners
11. Register a `window.addEventListener('beforeunload', ...)` handler that saves all dirty files to `localStorage`

